(Consumes the mathkit library through its `.lib` — the Vox consumption path
that arrives with plan 230 Stage A4. Until that lands this file will not
compile: the compiler does not yet emit or read `.lib` files, so `see` of a
`.lib` is a no-op and `add two numbers` below is an unknown function. It is
here so the full intended workflow lives in one place, and it will be re-run
against the finished compiler before this ships. The caller that runs today is
mathkit_driver.asm. See LANGUAGE.md, "Consuming a library".

  vox examples/mathkit_lib.vox --shared -o examples/libmathkit.so
  vox examples/mathkit_consumer.vox -o examples/mathkit_consumer
  ./examples/mathkit_consumer
  -> 7)

see "mathkit" version "1.0" from "./libmathkit.lib".

a number called "sum" is "add two numbers" of 3 and 4.
Print the sum.